---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_URL, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy policy of Solo Tax Desk: your income never leaves the page" description="What Solo Tax Desk processes: no cookie, no account, no email asked, no income figure sent anywhere, nothing passed to tax or formation firms. Your rights under the GDPR and US laws." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. Income, profit and filing status are sensitive: on many tax sites they are the price of the answer. Here they are computed in your browser and sent nowhere, and the site sets no cookie. The publisher is established in France, so the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to everything the site does, for every visitor; residents of US states with a consumer privacy law keep at least the rights below.</p>
    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>Every figure you type is used by the calculator inside your browser. "Copy share link" writes your inputs into the page address: anyone you send the link to can read them.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting logs</h3><p>GitHub, the host, records the IP address, time, page and browser of each request for security. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention: GitHub's policy.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h3>Cookie-free stability measurement</h3><p>Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited) is loaded in a mode that sets no cookie and does not link visits; it measures errors, load times and clicks that do nothing, with page content and typed values masked. Microsoft receives the technical request data, including the IP address. Legal basis: legitimate interest in a site that works (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object by blocking clarity.ms or by writing to us.</p></>
      : <><h3>No analytics</h3><p>No analytics, advertising or social media script is loaded today. Before any stability tool is switched on, this page will name it and explain how to refuse it.</p></>}
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write, we keep your address and message to answer and delete them three years after the last exchange. Please never send a Social Security number, an EIN or a tax return: we do not need them.</p>
    <h2>4. No sale, no leads</h2><p>We sell and share no personal information and pass nothing to accountants, tax software, payroll or formation companies.</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers</h2><p>GitHub, Inc. is in the United States; request data may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability and objection: write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, answer within one month. You may complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>The site is meant for adults and collects nothing from children.</p>
    <p>See the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>legal notice</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
